## Repeat the promotion-format variant

This is explicitly a changed opponent adapter, not an unmodified MinimalChess
repeat. Use the same native MinimalChess 0.6 release and runtime setup as above.
Create an executable shell shim, replacing the three absolute paths:

    #!/bin/sh
    exec /absolute/path/to/node /absolute/path/to/repo/scripts/uci-normalize.cjs --log /tmp/promotion-adjustments.jsonl -- '/absolute/path/to/MinimalChessEngine'

Set the shim as command in an opponents JSON with a single name
MinimalChess0.6-normalized and options ["option.Hash=32"]. Save this EPD line:

    8/P4pk1/6p1/3Bn3/4P3/4q2P/2p4P/Q6K w - -

Prepare a new run with --opponents pointing to that JSON, --games-per-opponent 2,
--concurrency 1 and --openings pointing to that EPD file, alongside the same
--fastchess and --revision flags used above; then run the printed command.
Use a fresh JSONL audit path for each run. Record SHA-256s of the native binary,
wrapper and shim, and preserve all adjustments and referee warnings. To enforce
those extra hashes automatically, add an additionalInputs object to that
opponent in campaign.json, mapping each absolute input path to its SHA-256.
The recorded diagnostic contains these hashes and its exact shim/wrapper.
For other engines, do not apply this workaround unless a specific format fault
has been diagnosed. Native-pipe integration and token-level checks run via the
two test-uci-normalize commands above.

